codex
The root cause is now concrete: this container’s `getpid()` returns the PID-namespace value, while `/proc` exposes host PIDs; Lean 4.22 resolves its executable via `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`, so it looks at a nonexistent path. I’m applying a narrow runtime shim that makes `getpid()` return `/proc/self`’s exposed PID, leaving Lean, Lake, the generated project, and candidate sources unchanged. I’ll record the shim and rerun the mandated trusted checks under it.
apply patch
patch: completed
/tmp/audit-work/lean-proc-pid-shim.c
